1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:04,930
Oh, what a lovely sound, Elisha.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:05,950
Thank you.

3
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:06,710
Whoops.

4
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:08,970
Whoa, I guess I'm not that good at the steel drum.

5
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,170
But my son, Wes, is very good.

6
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:14,750
He's taking lessons from my wife on our homemade steel drum.

7
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:18,790
But the other day, Wes didn't want to play his drum.

8
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:23,870
He told us that another kid at school said his drum sounded funny.

9
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:25,710
Oh, no, that is awful.

10
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:26,590
Yeah, I know.

11
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:27,750
It bothered me.

12
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:29,950
And I could tell it really bothered Wes, too.

13
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,410
I just didn't know what to say.

14
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:33,010
I was upset.

15
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:35,770
I realized I needed to take a pause.

16
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:38,170
That is a great idea.

17
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:40,610
Sometimes we need to take a breather.

18
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:44,910
Yeah, I need to understand how I felt and acknowledge how Wes felt.

19
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:51,030
Then I reminded him that he plays the steel drums because it connects to his ancestors.

20
00:00:51,410 --> 00:00:52,670
Oh, his Aunt Esther?

21
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:55,190
Oh, must be a wonderful woman.

22
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:57,250
No, no, no.

23
00:00:57,890 --> 00:01:00,150
Ancestors, where and who we come from.

24
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:05,970
You see, Wes has African-American roots from me and Caribbean roots from his mom.

25
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,130
Her parents come from Trinidad, where the steel drum is played.

26
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:11,010
From Trinidad, you say?

27
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:11,630
Yep.

28
00:01:11,870 --> 00:01:13,030
I reminded Wes of that.

29
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:15,310
I just needed a moment to gather myself.

30
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,690
See, you don't have to answer right away.

31
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,470
It's just important that you do answer.

32
00:01:19,730 --> 00:01:20,250
Right, Grover?

33
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:22,820
Right, Grover?

34
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,600
No, I am pausing.

35
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,660
Remember, you do not have to answer right away.

36
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,360
You just said that.

37
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,020
Yeah, I did.

